---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';

const services = [
  {
    id: 'interior',
    title: 'Interior Painting',
    icon: '🖌️',
    photo: '/photos/interior-hallway-painted.jpg',
    photoAlt: 'Interior hallway with freshly painted olive walls and hardwood floors',
    body: [
      'A fresh coat of paint is one of the fastest ways to transform a space — but the difference between a good paint job and a great one comes down to preparation. Ingersoll Painting treats every interior project the same way: furniture moved, floors protected, trim taped, and surfaces properly primed before a drop of finish coat goes on.',
      'We handle walls, ceilings, trim, doors, and closets. We work with you on color selection and can advise on Benjamin Moore products that will hold up in high-traffic areas, kitchens, bathrooms, and anywhere else that sees daily use. Every job gets two coats minimum unless the existing color is a near-match.',
      'When we\'re done, we do a final walkthrough with you to make sure everything is exactly right. That\'s the 1-year workmanship warranty in action - we stand behind the finish.',
    ],
    features: ['Walls, ceilings & trim', 'Color consultation', 'Benjamin Moore products', 'Full prep & protection', '1-year warranty'],
  },
  {
    id: 'exterior',
    title: 'Exterior Painting',
    icon: '🏠',
    photo: '/photos/exterior-lakefront-house.jpg',
    photoAlt: 'Exterior painting on lakefront home with white siding and dark lower level',
    body: [
      'Exterior painting in Central New York takes more than a good brush - it takes the right products and the right prep. Ingersoll Painting uses Benjamin Moore Woodluxe and High Build formulas built to handle the freeze-thaw cycles, UV exposure, and moisture that come with Oswego County winters.',
      'Every exterior job starts with a thorough inspection: loose paint scraped, bare wood primed, caulk replaced around windows and trim, and any rot addressed before we touch a brush. Painting over a bad surface just delays the problem - we fix it first.',
      'We handle siding, trim, soffits, fascia, shutters, doors, and porches. We protect your landscaping, windows, and hardscape throughout the job and clean up completely when we\'re finished.',
    ],
    features: ['Full surface prep & scraping', 'Benjamin Moore Woodluxe & High Build', 'Caulking & minor rot repair', 'Siding, trim, soffits & fascia', 'Porches & shutters'],
  },
  {
    id: 'decks',
    title: 'Deck Building, Staining & Pressure Washing',
    icon: '🏗️',
    photo: '/photos/deck-stain-before-after.jpg',
    photoAlt: 'Deck staining before and after - weathered gray boards restored to rich brown',
    body: [
      'We build decks from the ground up and restore existing ones that have seen better days. New builds use pressure-treated lumber, composite decking, or cedar depending on your budget and preference - all framed and finished to code with proper footings, ledger attachment, and railing.',
      'For existing decks, we pressure wash first to strip off dirt, mildew, and oxidized wood fibers, then apply a solid or semi-transparent stain that soaks into the wood and protects it from the inside. A properly stained deck in Oswego County can go 3-5 years before it needs attention again.',
      'Pressure washing is also available as a standalone service for decks, driveways, siding, and concrete - a good first step before any painting or staining project.',
    ],
    features: ['New deck construction', 'Deck restoration & repair', 'Pressure washing', 'Solid & semi-transparent staining', 'Composite & wood decking'],
  },
  {
    id: 'cabinets',
    title: 'Cabinet Refinishing',
    icon: '🚪',
    photo: '/photos/cabinets-blue-gray-kitchen.jpg',
    photoAlt: 'Two-tone blue and gray kitchen cabinet refinishing - finished result',
    body: [
      'Kitchen cabinet replacement costs $15,000-$50,000. Cabinet refinishing from Ingersoll Painting costs a fraction of that and delivers a finish you can\'t tell from new - because we spray it the same way a cabinet shop would.',
      'Every door and drawer front comes off. Hardware is removed. Surfaces are sanded, degreased, and primed. We spray 2-3 coats of finish in your chosen color - Benjamin Moore Advance is our standard recommendation, a waterborne alkyd that cures hard and levels beautifully. Then everything goes back on with new hardware if you want it.',
      'We\'ve done full kitchens in a single color, two-tone combinations with a contrasting island, and everything in between. The before-and-after on a cabinet job is one of the most dramatic transformations in home renovation.',
    ],
    features: ['All doors & drawers removed', 'Full sand, degrease & prime', 'Spray finish - Benjamin Moore Advance', 'Single color or two-tone', 'Hardware installation available'],
  },
  {
    id: 'drywall',
    title: 'Drywall Installation & Repair',
    icon: '🔧',
    photo: '/photos/interior-mudroom-barn-doors.jpg',
    photoAlt: 'Finished interior with clean drywall and built-in shelving',
    body: [
      'Clean drywall is the foundation of a good paint job - and Ingersoll Painting handles both sides of it. We repair everything from small nail holes and drywall cracks to water-damaged sections and full room installations.',
      'For repairs, we match the existing texture as closely as possible so patches disappear under paint. For new installs, we hang, tape, mud, and sand to a smooth finish ready for primer. We also do skim coating over existing walls to remove texture and get a modern flat finish.',
      'Popcorn ceiling removal is a popular add-on - we wet the texture, scrape it clean, skim coat if needed, and leave you with a flat ceiling that looks like it was never textured. Ask about bundling drywall work with a paint job for the best pricing.',
    ],
    features: ['Patch & repair (all sizes)', 'Full drywall installation', 'Skim coating', 'Popcorn ceiling removal', 'Texture matching'],
  },
  {
    id: 'epoxy',
    title: 'Epoxy Floor Coatings',
    icon: '✨',
    body: [
      'Epoxy floor coatings turn a bare concrete floor into a durable, cleanable surface that looks sharp and holds up to heavy use. Garages, basements, and commercial floors all benefit from a proper epoxy system.',
      'The prep work is everything with epoxy. We grind or acid-etch the concrete to open the surface, fill cracks and control joints, and apply a moisture-blocking primer before the epoxy goes down. A cheap roll-on kit from the hardware store peels because the prep was skipped - we don\'t skip it.',
      'Standard finish is a solid color base coat with broadcast color flakes and a clear polyaspartic topcoat that resists UV yellowing, hot tire pickup, and chemical spills. Most residential garage floors are done in one day with 24-hour return to light traffic.',
    ],
    features: ['Concrete grinding & prep', 'Crack filling & priming', 'Full broadcast flake system', 'Polyaspartic topcoat', 'Garages, basements & commercial'],
  },
  {
    id: 'basement',
    title: 'Basement Remodeling',
    icon: '🏘️',
    photo: '/photos/basement-remodel-framing.jpg',
    photoAlt: 'Basement remodel framing in progress',
    body: [
      'An unfinished basement is the most underused square footage in your home. Ingersoll Painting does full basement finishes - framing, insulation, drywall, flooring, paint, and trim - turning raw concrete space into livable rooms.',
      'We work from your floor plan or help you lay one out. Typical basement projects include a main living area, a bedroom or two, a bathroom rough-in, and a utility/storage area. We coordinate the work so everything happens in the right sequence and nothing has to be redone.',
      'Basement work is priced by the project, not the hour. You get a written estimate before anything starts, and we stick to it.',
    ],
    features: ['Framing & insulation', 'Drywall & painting', 'Flooring installation', 'Trim & door installation', 'Full finish, top to bottom'],
  },
  {
    id: 'bathroom',
    title: 'Bathroom Remodeling',
    icon: '🚿',
    photo: '/photos/bathroom-tile-install.jpg',
    photoAlt: 'Bathroom tile floor installation in progress',
    body: [
      'Bathrooms are small spaces that take a disproportionate amount of skill to do right. Waterproofing, tile work, and tight tolerances matter more here than anywhere else in the house. Ingersoll Painting handles full bathroom renovations - demo, tile, vanity, fixtures, paint, and finish.',
      'We do floor and wall tile including large-format and wood-look planks. Vanity swaps, toilet replacement, mirror and light fixture installation, and caulk/grout work are all in scope. We also do bathroom paint using moisture-resistant products that won\'t peel or blister.',
      'Whether you want a full gut-and-rebuild or a cosmetic refresh, we can scope it out and give you a written estimate. Most cosmetic bathroom renovations are done in 3-5 days.',
    ],
    features: ['Floor & wall tile', 'Vanity & fixture installation', 'Moisture-resistant paint', 'Caulk & grout work', 'Full gut-and-rebuild available'],
  },
  {
    id: 'commercial',
    title: 'Commercial Painting & Renovation',
    icon: '🏢',
    body: [
      'Ingersoll Painting works with property owners, landlords, and businesses throughout Oswego, Onondaga, and Cayuga counties on commercial and multi-unit painting projects. We\'ve done apartment complexes, office buildings, government facilities, and retail spaces.',
      'Commercial work requires scheduling discipline and efficiency - we understand that vacant units cost money and occupied buildings need minimal disruption. We can work off-hours, phase projects across occupied units, and turn around apartment turnovers on tight timelines.',
      'All commercial work is fully insured with certificates of insurance available on request. We can handle the paint, or supply-and-install depending on the project.',
    ],
    features: ['Apartment turnovers', 'Office & retail spaces', 'Government & institutional', 'Off-hours scheduling available', 'COI provided on request'],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Painting & Renovation Services | Ingersoll Painting LLC"
  description="Interior painting, exterior painting, cabinet refinishing, deck building, drywall, epoxy floors, basement and bathroom remodeling. Serving Oswego, Onondaga, and Cayuga counties since 1978."
>

  <!-- Page Hero -->
  <section class="bg-gray-900 py-16 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center">
      <p
        class="text-[#2baae1] uppercase tracking-widest text-sm mb-3"
        style="font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.15em;"
      >
        What We Do
      </p>
      <h1
        class="text-white text-6xl sm:text-7xl lg:text-8xl leading-none mb-5"
        style="font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.04em;"
      >
        Our Services
      </h1>
      <p
        class="text-gray-400 text-xl max-w-2xl mx-auto"
        style="font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif; font-size: 1.15rem;"
      >
        Painting is where we started. Renovation is where we've grown. One crew, one call, one company you can count on.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Content: sticky sidebar + service sections -->
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 flex gap-12 items-start">

    <!-- Sticky sidebar nav — desktop only -->
    <aside class="hidden lg:block w-52 shrink-0 sticky top-24 self-start">
      <p
        class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 mb-3"
        style="font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.2em;"
      >
        Jump to
      </p>
      <nav aria-label="Services in-page navigation">
        <ul class="space-y-0.5">
          {services.map(s => (
            <li>
              <a
                href={`#${s.id}`}
                class="flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-500 hover:text-[#2baae1] py-2 px-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-50 transition-colors"
                style="font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif; font-size: 0.95rem;"
              >
                <span aria-hidden="true">{s.icon}</span>
                {s.title}
              </a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </nav>
      <div class="mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-gray-100">
        <a
          href="/contact"
          class="block text-center bg-[#2baae1] hover:bg-[#1e8fc4] text-white font-medium py-3 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors"
          style="font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif; font-size: 1rem;"
        >
          Free Estimate
        </a>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <!-- Service sections -->
    <div class="flex-1 min-w-0 space-y-20">
      {services.map((s, i) => (
        <section id={s.id} class="scroll-mt-28">

          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
            <span class="text-4xl" aria-hidden="true">{s.icon}</span>
            <h2
              class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl text-gray-900 leading-none"
              style="font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.05em;"
            >
              {s.title}
            </h2>
          </div>

          {s.photo && (
            <div class="mb-7 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-lg">
              <img
                src={s.photo}
                alt={s.photoAlt}
                class="w-full object-cover max-h-72"
                loading="lazy"
                width="900"
                height="288"
              />
            </div>
          )}

          <div class="space-y-4 mb-7">
            {s.body.map(para => (
              <p
                class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed"
                style="font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif; font-size: 1.1rem;"
              >
                {para}
              </p>
            ))}
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6 items-start">
            <ul class="flex-1 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
              {s.features.map(f => (
                <li
                  class="flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-700"
                  style="font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif; font-size: 1.05rem;"
                >
                  <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-[#2baae1] shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
                  </svg>
                  {f}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
            <a
              href="/contact"
              class="shrink-0 bg-[#2baae1] hover:bg-[#1e8fc4] text-white font-medium px-7 py-3 rounded-lg transition-colors whitespace-nowrap"
              style="font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif; font-size: 1.05rem;"
            >
              Request an Estimate
            </a>
          </div>

          {i < services.length - 1 && (
            <hr class="mt-16 border-gray-100" />
          )}
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>

  <CtaBand
    heading="Not Sure Where to Start?"
    subtext="Call or send a message and we'll walk through the project with you. Free estimates, no pressure."
    primaryLabel="Get Free Estimate"
    primaryHref="/contact"
    secondaryLabel="Call (315) 952-8259"
    secondaryHref="tel:+13159528259"
  />

</BaseLayout>
